{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms","id":113648,"title":"[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-15T16:47:23-07:00","id":113648,"title":"[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms","content":"Wherein I gaze into the future and write charms for a system I haven't seen yet. This is how I deal with boredom. <br /> <br /> Melee/Brawl:<br /> <br /> <b>Dojo of the Mind</b><br /> The Solar plays out the results of a battle in her mind to create the best opportunity to strike. When activating this Charm, the Solar selects a target. This Charm provides the following effects:<br /> - The Solar's attacks take place only in her mind. Substitute Dexterity for Intelligence and Strength for Wits when rolling attacks and damage.<br /> - The Solar's attacks gains long range.<br /> - The Solar may defend herself and move normally, but may not attack anyone other than her current target.<br /> - The Solar cannot use lethal attacks or Gambits, but can use all her other powers. The Solar's target may defend herself normally.<br /> - The Solar's attacks gain [momentum] as normal. However, they cannot cause effects which require physical contact, such as poison and knockback.<br /> - If the Charm's target attacks the Solar, the Solar immediately gains a clash attack against her.<br /> <br /> Medicine:<br /> <br /> <b>Serpent-Killing Toxin</b><br /> The Solar gains the ability to manipulate poisons and diseases against each other. When treating a patient suffering from two or more poisons or diseases at the same time, the Solar can elect to cure some or all of them all simultaneously. The difficulty of the treatment is equal to the highest difficulty of the diseases or poisons the Solar wishes to cure, plus 1 for each additional disease or poison.<br /> <br /> Larceny:<br /> <br /> <b>Midnight Prowler's Entrance</b><br /> When the Solar enters a building or encampment which she has already scouted, this Charm provides the following benefits:<br /> - If the Solar attempts to physically break a wall or door in order gain access to the building, she converts a number of damage dice equal to her Larceny into automatic successes.<br /> - Within the scouted area, hostile characters who move towards the Solar or her allies do not count 10s as two successes when rolling combat movement dice. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T00:17:19-07:00","id":113889,"title":"","content":"Inexplicably I like Serpent-Killing Toxin the best. It's fairly mundane but it's awesome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/46-oramus","name":"Oramus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar46_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T00:34:03-07:00","id":113898,"title":"","content":"I agree with Oramus, Serpent-Killing Toxin is pretty great.<br /> <br /> I'm really not a fan of Dojo of the Mind ... it seems like an attempt to take the abilities most directly plugged into the close combat engine and make them esoteric. In particular I'm against the long range effect, and I think the 'no physical contact' effect is weird and difficult to adjudicate. <br /> <br /> I could either take or leave Midnight Prowler's Entrance, depending on the specifics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T02:35:30-07:00","id":113932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms?p=113898#post113898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really not a fan of Dojo of the Mind ... it seems like an attempt to take the abilities most directly plugged into the close combat engine and make them esoteric. In particular I'm against the long range effect, and I think the 'no physical contact' effect is weird and difficult to adjudicate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how the no physical contact thing is weird. You're beating up someone in your mind, obviously that's not going to let you poison them. Or wound them or do much of anything at all. Except apparently gain momentum from... your analysis of your opponent's fighting style, I guess?<br /> <br /> I'm kind of amused you use Wits as the Power stat and Intelligence as the Finesse stat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T03:31:39-07:00","id":113950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms?p=113932#post113932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how the no physical contact thing is weird. You're beating up someone in your mind, obviously that's not going to let you poison them. Or wound them or do much of anything at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>If an opponent uses a Charm to defend themselves in your mind, does it cost them any Essence? If your attack on them (that isn't really happening) allow them to trigger other Charms such as counter attacks? If they target characters other than you?<br /> <br /> 'All of this is really happening in my head' Charms are problematic. If you want a mental-based Charm that allows you to build momentum there must be easier ways. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T06:26:03-07:00","id":114004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms?p=113898#post113898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really not a fan of Dojo of the Mind ... it seems like an attempt to take the abilities most directly plugged into the close combat engine and make them esoteric. In particular I'm against the long range effect, and I think the 'no physical contact' effect is weird and difficult to adjudicate.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's meant to model fights where two people just stare at each other for three hours before attacking once and ending the fight in one blow. There's just no straightforward way to actually do it. The Solar using it has to be able to defend, or else it's suicidal. The Solar using it has to be able to attack normally, or else it'd be boring. The Solar's attack has to include physical effects, but not manifest them, because there's no physical attack. The target of the charm has to defend, or else you can't resolve combat or the Solar is just burning motes. I just can't see a way out of all the clutter.<br /> <br /> I'm assuming you could get the same general effect by taking Aim actions for a few dozen rounds, but that's not exactly exciting.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, I originally couldn't decide if the effect should be a Charm or a Merit, but ultimately decided that it should require a level of mastery that should be beyond mortals. You could probably take out the side-benefits, maybe leave Intelligence and Wits in to substitute for physical attributes, and treat the whole fight as one long stunt that just happens in people's heads until one of them goes for a killing blow. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":54,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","user":"Tiresias","date":". 04-16-2014, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T06:43:14-07:00","id":114015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms?p=114004#post114004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm assuming you could get the same general effect by taking Aim actions for a few dozen rounds, but that's not exactly exciting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you pretty much answer the question here, this Charm should be supplemental to an Aim action, allowing you to make some sort of roll and add momentum according to the result. Is this as exciting? Maybe not, but it avoids all the complex interactions that arise when you want to stare intently at your opponent for three hours while a battle unfolds in your mind and he'd rather just punch you in the face. <br /> <br /> Telling your opponent that all his defensive actions are really only happening in your head, but they cost his resources anyhow? Bad juju.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T07:08:06-07:00","id":114038,"title":"","content":"How about a Charm where you watch your opponent fight/spar for a set amount of time, then the next time you fight them you can start with bonus momentum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/46-oramus","name":"Oramus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar46_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T07:40:41-07:00","id":114053,"title":"","content":"I wonder if they're going to keep Meditative Battlefield Escalation...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T08:22:30-07:00","id":114083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oramus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms?p=114038#post114038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about a Charm where you watch your opponent fight/spar for a set amount of time, then the next time you fight them you can start with bonus momentum?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given what's been said about the combat system and support abilities I'd imagine there will be plenty of ways to get momentum without hitting people. This one is just problematic because of the whole 'I'm hitting you, but totally not hitting you, but still levying costs on you just as though I was hitting you' part. And also the range. I really don't like that in Melee/MA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T14:00:55-07:00","id":114321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oramus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms?p=114038#post114038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about a Charm where you watch your opponent fight/spar for a set amount of time, then the next time you fight them you can start with bonus momentum?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a lot easier to conceptualize.<br /> <br /> Lore:<br /> <br /> <b>Victorious Stratagem Contemplation</b><br /> The Solar studies her opponents in order to understand her weaknesses. The Solar activates this charm when her nemesis rolls battle against someone else. If the Solar witnesses the fight from its beginning to its resolution and takes no other action during that time, she gains (Lore?) momentum the next time she rolls join battle to fight the charm's target. <br /> <br /> Stealth:<br /> <br /> <b>Wing of the Swooping Owl</b><br /> While the Solar is engaged in battle and hidden, he may select one of her opponents as this charm's target. For every round in which the Solar remains hidden from the target, the Solar gains X additional momentum. This charm lasts until the target becomes aware of the Solar. <br /> <br /> Melee: <br /> <br /> <b>Steel Trapper's Feint</b><br /> Upon activating this charm, the Solar selects a target and a combat ability. Whenever the charm's target would gain momentum by attacking the Solar with that ability, the momentum she gains is reduced by 1, to a minimum of 1. <br /> <br /> And an unrelated Lore charm:<br /> <br /> <b>Philosophical Logic Meditation</b><br /> Drawing upon her knowledge of debate and argumentation, the Solar can expose the flaws in her opponent's discourse. Upon activating this charm, the Solar gains a Defining Principle which opposes an opponent's arguments. This Intimacy lasts until the end of the scene and the charm can only be used once per scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T16:01:17-07:00","id":114383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms#post113648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Melee/Brawl:<br /> <br /> <b>Dojo of the Mind</b><br /> The Solar plays out the results of a battle in her mind to create the best opportunity to strike. When activating this Charm, the Solar selects a target. This Charm provides the following effects:<br /> - The Solar's attacks take place only in her mind. Substitute Dexterity for Intelligence and Strength for Wits when rolling attacks and damage.<br /> - The Solar's attacks gains long range.<br /> - The Solar may defend herself and move normally, but may not attack anyone other than her current target.<br /> - The Solar cannot use lethal attacks or Gambits, but can use all her other powers. The Solar's target may defend herself normally.<br /> - The Solar's attacks gain [momentum] as normal. However, they cannot cause effects which require physical contact, such as poison and knockback.<br /> - If the Charm's target attacks the Solar, the Solar immediately gains a clash attack against her.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty neat, and once you've got your hands on the whole combat system, I think you'll quickly realize the mechanical verve this needs to really deliver on the concept. In terms of Ability choice, I think Melee will fit much better than Brawl, given that Brawl is a very two-fisted, bloody-knuckled thing (and that it already has its own suite of effects that manipulate similar elements in its own distinctive way). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Medicine:<br /> <br /> <b>Serpent-Killing Toxin</b><br /> The Solar gains the ability to manipulate poisons and diseases against each other. When treating a patient suffering from two or more poisons or diseases at the same time, the Solar can elect to cure some or all of them all simultaneously. The difficulty of the treatment is equal to the highest difficulty of the diseases or poisons the Solar wishes to cure, plus 1 for each additional disease or poison. </div> </div> </div>I <i>think</i> the timing rules for treating diseases/poisons would make this irrelevant most of the time, although it's possible I'm misremembering or something's been tweaked in editing. Sorry <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Larceny:<br /> <br /> <b>Midnight Prowler's Entrance</b><br /> When the Solar enters a building or encampment which she has already scouted, this Charm provides the following benefits:<br /> - If the Solar attempts to physically break a wall or door in order gain access to the building, she converts a number of damage dice equal to her Larceny into automatic successes.<br /> - Within the scouted area, hostile characters who move towards the Solar or her allies do not count 10s as two successes when rolling combat movement dice. </div> </div> </div>The logic of &quot;casing the joint to gain bonuses during a later heist&quot; is a fruitful one. I'm not sure if combat-focused benefits fully make sense\u2014the name had me expecting it'd be buffing Stealth.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T21:31:10-07:00","id":114529,"title":"","content":"I do hope that the Disease/Poison rule don't make my head hurt when I read them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T06:10:45-07:00","id":114675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms?p=114383#post114383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The logic of &quot;casing the joint to gain bonuses during a later heist&quot; is a fruitful one. I'm not sure if combat-focused benefits fully make sense\u2014the name had me expecting it'd be buffing Stealth.</div> </div> </div> </div>My naming sense sucks and &quot;Break Into The Building Through The Door That's Really Far Away From Where All The Guards Are So It Takes Them Longer To Get To You And Stab You In The Face Prana&quot; would have soaked up the word count faster than She Who Lives In Her Name does. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, more charms.<br /> <br /> Bureaucracy: <br /> <br /> <b>Officious Seal Technique</b><br /> The Solar may use this charm against other members of an organization to which he belongs, either permanently or temporarily. The members gain an Intimacy towards the Solar that is identical to the Intimacy they hold towards the organization. <br /> <br /> Craft: <br /> <br /> <b>Art of the Beguiling Tribute</b><br /> This charm can be used when crafting a gift or bribe for a specific person. When the Solar presents the gift to its intended recipient, that person gains a Major Tie of adoration towards the Solar for one scene. <br /> <br /> <b>Craft of Love</b><br /> The Solar's passion drives his artifice. When rolling to craft an object specifically for someone towards whom the Solar holds a positive Minor Tie, the Solar counts 9s as two successes. If the Intimacy is a positive Major Tie, 8s count as two successes as well and if the Intimacy is a positive Defining Tie, 7s also count as two successes. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T06:17:55-07:00","id":115248,"title":"","content":"Integrity: <br /> <br /> <b>Tempting Demon's Evidence</b><br /> Becoming aware of the flaw in her beliefs, the Solar can temporarily suppress them. When activating this Charm, the Solar replaces one of her Intimacies with an opposing Intimacy. The effect lasts so long as the Charm is active. <br /> <br /> Larceny:<br /> <br /> <b>Blade-Pilfering Practice</b><br /> This Charm allows the Solar to perform a disarm attack by rolling Dexterity + Larceny. It can also be used to steal munitions from quivers and such during combat. <br /> <br /> <b>Corpse-Hiding Technique</b><br /> This Charm can be used to help the Solar hide a dead body. People will not find the body unless they are specifically looking for a corpse, nor will they notice the victim's disappearance unless they have a specific need for her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T07:54:09-07:00","id":115274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms?p=115248#post115248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Corpse-Hiding Technique</b><br /> This Charm can be used to help the Solar hide a dead body. People will not find the body unless they are specifically looking for a corpse, nor will they notice the victim's disappearance unless they have a specific need for her.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems more Abyssal to me. Solars might have an &quot;Hide stuff perfectly, even from people's memory&quot;-charm which also allows them to hide bodies, but a specific &quot;Hide corpses&quot;-charm doesn't seem to fit their thematics.<br /> <br /> Oh, and a charm I'd love to see?<br /> <b>Sun Blends Out The Sky Method</b> (Or &quot;Pay no attention to the man behind the curtain Prana&quot;... something like that)<br /> Ability: Stealth, or maybe Larceny, or maybe even Presence.<br /> I... can't actually make up any specific rules for it, but this charm would allow a Solar to hide his allies by drawing all the attention to himself. Ideally, even in an otherwise completely empty room, his enemy would only see him, and no one else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","user":"Dusk Shine","date":". 04-18-2014, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T11:56:46-07:00","id":115437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms?p=115274#post115274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems more Abyssal to me. Solars might have an &quot;Hide stuff perfectly, even from people's memory&quot;-charm which also allows them to hide bodies, but a specific &quot;Hide corpses&quot;-charm doesn't seem to fit their thematics.</div> </div> </div> </div>For some reason, whenever I play a stealth game, I end up having to hide bodies all over, so I thought that sort of charm would make sneaking around more convenient.<br /> <br /> Occult: <br /> <br /> <b>Finding the Spirit's Abode</b><br /> So long as the Solar knows the name of a god or possesses one of its belongings or idols, this Charm allows the Solar to unerringly find the entrance to the spirit's sanctum. <br /> <br /> <b>Demon-Hunter's Instinct</b><br /> Whenever a spirit uses one of its Charms to harm a mortal within (Essence) miles of the Solar, the Solar may roll Perception + Occult to learn the precise location of both the spirit and its victim. <br /> <br /> <b>Otherworldly Banquet's Etiquette</b><br /> When the Solar attempts to leverage the customs of the Fair Folk, spirits or the undead against them, she may reroll a number of unsuccessful dice equal to her Occult rating. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T12:18:54-07:00","id":115453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms?p=115437#post115437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For some reason, whenever I play a stealth game, I end up having to hide bodies all over, so I thought that sort of charm would make sneaking around more convenient.</div> </div> </div> </div>I *did* notice that it basically allows video game stealth.<br /> &quot;Sure, I killed half of the guards by now, but since no one saw me, nobody thinks anything is wrong.&quot; <br /> <br /> Not that I should complain, I prefer the &quot;unrealistic glibness&quot; approach to infiltration. <br /> &quot;Yes, you found me, but I can't be an enemy. No enemy could sneak past our guards. And even if an enemy could sneak past our guards, then he'd be far to sneaky to be found by you. So, obviously, I have a perfectly valid reason to be here. But it's secret, so I can't tell you. Now don't mention me to anyone else, because it's a secret.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T15:13:38-07:00","id":116140,"title":"","content":"Resistance:<br /> <br /> <b>Manna of Flesh and Will</b><br /> Whenever the Solar would gain a point of Willpower, she may instead satiate herself as if she had eaten and slept enough to last a number of days equal to her Essence without requiring further rest or sustenance.<br /> <br /> <b>Fist-Breaking Mountain Stance</b><br /> If the Solar is hit by a close-range Melee or Brawl Attack, but takes no damage, she may initiate a counterattack against her opponent using nothing but her armour. The Solar rolls Stamina + Resistance to hit and adds Strength to her damage. Treat the Solar's armour as a weapon of its size and give it the Blunt damage tag. This attack may be enhanced by Brawl charms.<br /> <br /> Performance: <br /> <br /> <b>Orchestral War Hymn</b><br /> The Solar may spend X motes to add his Performance rating to his join battle roll. In addition, whenever the Solar joins roll battle, the environment joins together to play a battle song iconic to the Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":54,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","user":"Tiresias","date":". 04-19-2014, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T20:04:28-07:00","id":116300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusk Shine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms?p=115453#post115453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I *did* notice that it basically allows video game stealth.<br /> &quot;Sure, I killed half of the guards by now, but since no one saw me, nobody thinks anything is wrong.&quot;<br /> <br /> Not that I should complain, I prefer the &quot;unrealistic glibness&quot; approach to infiltration.<br /> &quot;Yes, you found me, but I can't be an enemy. No enemy could sneak past our guards. And even if an enemy could sneak past our guards, then he'd be far to sneaky to be found by you. So, obviously, I have a perfectly valid reason to be here. But it's secret, so I can't tell you. Now don't mention me to anyone else, because it's a secret.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>My favourite thing about Crimson Razor Wind, from the Infernals preview, is that people and things destroyed by it are completely erased and everyone forgets they ever existed, so it's <i>fantastic</i> for this and wholly deserves to be a Stealth charm in spite of being an attack...<i>but </i>you forget that you killed people with it as well, so you can't actually tell whether you've infiltrated unnoticed or killed a bunch of people nobody remembers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T16:17:08-07:00","id":116712,"title":"","content":"Linguistics:<br /> <br /> <b>Undisputed Authorial Word</b><br /> The Solar becomes the absolute authority on anything she writes. This charm supplements an attempt to erode a minor or major principle through written communication. If the attempt succeeds, the principle is not weakened, but the target cannot apply its benefits to resist the Solar's social influence. The principle's drawbacks always apply in full. <br /> <br /> <b>Discourse of False Logic</b><br /> This charm allows the Solar to interfere with another character's attempts to influence a third party's intimacies. If the other character's roll is successful, the Solar may roll Manipulation + Linguistics. If the Solar obtains more successes on the roll, she may change which of the third party's intimacies is being influence, although its strength must be equal to that of the original intimacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T00:19:57-07:00","id":116851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms?p=116140#post116140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Manna of Flesh and Will</b><br /> Whenever the Solar would gain a point of Willpower, she may instead satiate herself as if she had eaten and slept enough to last a number of days equal to her Essence without requiring further rest or sustenance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the concept is about sustaining the body with &quot;food of the mind&quot;, instead of just being tough and ignoring your hunger, I'd actually be tempted to put it in some other Ability... Integrity? Lore?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T11:11:55-07:00","id":117048,"title":"","content":"War:<br /> <br /> <b>Unerring Tactical Foresight</b><br /> A single glance is enough for the Lawgiver to gain complete insight of a battlefield. When a battle group under the Solar's command joins battle, the Solar may declare a number of combat rounds up to her War rating. If the battle group under the Solar's command performs a lethal attack on another combat group on that exact round, they gain (6 - Rounds chosen) dice of additional damage. <br /> <br /> <b>Unleashing the Radiant Legion</b><br /> If a battle group under the Solar's command makes a lethal attack against another battle group and is at negative momentum relative to its target, the Solar may spend X willpower and Y motes to add her Essence rating to the battle group's effective momentum. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T16:19:47-07:00","id":121284,"title":"","content":"I've decided to think up one new charm per day, every day, until Ex3 is in my hands. Abilities will be chosen randomly.<br /> <br /> Investigation:<br /> <br /> <b>Lawman's Sudden Realization</b><br /> If the Solar fails an Investigation roll to identify the culprit of a crime and the criminal begins to plan a second crime in the Solar's general vicinity, the Solar may reroll the Investigation roll in order to gain sudden insight into the culprit's behaviour and stop her before the second crime is committed. In addition, if the Solar uses the Investigation Excellency to enhance the roll, the excellency's cost is reduce by one mote for each of the culprit's crime scenes that the Solar has investigated, successfully or not.<br /> <br /> <b>Lawman's Sudden Realization 2.0</b><br /> A successful Wits + Investigation roll automatically allows the Lawgiver to know if two crimes were committed by the same person. In addition, when investigating serial criminals, the Solar reduces the cost of the Investigation Excellency by one mote per crime scene she has investigated. Finally, if the Solar has investigated (6 - Investigation) of the culprit's crime scenes, she may roll Wits + Investigation against the culprits Manipulation + Larceny in order to predict the culprit's next crime in the Solar's general area, if the criminal is planning one. If the roll fails, the Solar may try again after investigating the culprit's next crime scene. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":54,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","user":"Tiresias","date":". 05-03-2014, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T05:53:25-07:00","id":121649,"title":"","content":"War:<br /> <br /> <b>Steel Wall Encirclement</b><br /> When the Solar commands a combat group against another, she may user her troops to seal the enemy's movements. The Solar and the enemy commander make an opposed Wits + War roll. Each of the Solar's net successes applies an external penalty of 1 to the enemy force's combat movement. This charm lasts for a number of actions equal to the Solar's war rating, but ends immediately if the Solar's troops move.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T07:39:46-07:00","id":121691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms?p=121284#post121284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've decided to think up one new charm per day, every day, until Ex3 is in my hands. Abilities will be chosen randomly. Investigation: <b>Lawman's Sudden Realization</b> If the Solar fails an Investigation roll to identify the culprit of a crime and the criminal begins to plan a second crime in the Solar's general vicinity, the Solar may reroll the Investigation roll in order to gain sudden insight into the culprit's behaviour and stop her before the second crime is committed. In addition, if the Solar uses the Investigation Excellency to enhance the roll, the excellency's cost is reduce by one mote for each of the culprit's crime scenes that the Solar has investigated, successfully or not.</div> </div> </div> </div> I love this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T06:22:46-07:00","id":122294,"title":"","content":"Sail:<br /> <br /> <b>Reef-Crushing Wave</b><br /> Whenever a natural obstacle such as a rock, reef or cliff would damage the Solar's ship, the Lawgiver may pay X motes to ram the obstacle instead. Roll Wits + Sail to attack and use the Solar's Essence rating instead of strength when rolling damage. Treat the ship as a heavy weapon with the Blunt tag. If the attack is successful and does damage, the Solar's ship takes no damage from the obstacle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T09:40:34-07:00","id":122407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms?p=115248#post115248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Becoming aware of the flaw in her beliefs, the Solar can temporarily suppress them. When activating this Charm, the Solar replaces one of her Intimacies with an opposing Intimacy. The effect lasts so long as the Charm is active.</div> </div> </div> </div>Geebus. Given how central intimacies are to the Influence system this falls on the line between 'Solar awesome' and 'Sidereal meta-weirdness'. My instinct would be to fall on the Sidereal side. Solars should carry the strength of their convictions, no matter what.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms?p=115248#post115248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This Charm allows the Solar to perform a disarm attack by rolling Dexterity + Larceny. It can also be used to steal munitions from quivers and such during combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be a very low-level Solar Charm. Depending on how ability-swapping is 'priced' it may not even be worth a Solar Charm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms?p=115248#post115248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This Charm can be used to help the Solar hide a dead body. People will not find the body unless they are specifically looking for a corpse, nor will they notice the victim's disappearance unless they have a specific need for her.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are at least two abilities more suited for this effect than Larceny, as regards Solars. This would be an excellent Abyssal Larceny Charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","user":"SuddenThunder","date":".  Fixed bad tagging 04-30-2014, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T07:09:32-07:00","id":123125,"title":"","content":"Medicine:<br /> <br /> <b>Remedy of Exalted Resilience</b><br /> The Solar's supernatural healing skills persist in her absence. When treating a wounded mortal, the Solar may commit a number of motes equal to the lesser of her Intelligence + Medicine or the patient's Stamina + Resistance. So long as the motes remain committed, the patient may apply the benefit of the Resistance Excellency to all attempts to resist poison, disease or death from grievous wounds, adding a number of dice equal to the number of motes committed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T06:55:41-07:00","id":123754,"title":"","content":"Resistance:<br /> <br /> <b>Weapon-Trapping Stone Flesh Crevasse</b><br /> Whenever the Solar takes damage from a close-range weapon, she may spend X motes and roll Strength + Resistance to disarm her attacker. The weapon remains sealed by the Solar's muscles for a number of actions equal to her Essence, but someone attacking the Solar with Brawl may choose to forgo a successful attack's damage in order to pull the weapon out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T07:11:39-07:00","id":123760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms?p=123754#post123754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resistance:<br /> <br /> <b>Weapon-Trapping Stone Flesh Crevasse</b><br /> Whenever the Solar takes damage from a close-range weapon, she may spend X motes and roll Strength + Resistance to disarm her attacker. The weapon remains sealed by the Solar's muscles for a number of actions equal to her Essence, but someone attacking the Solar with Brawl may choose to forgo a successful attack's damage in order to pull the weapon out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, isn't this a little bit too Kimbery/Metagaos Infernal ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T07:25:28-07:00","id":123769,"title":"","content":"Maybe. I was inspired by Kenshirou flexing his muscles to seal his wounds and stop his bleeding, which seems like a Solar thing. <br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> You know what would have made a better charm? Flexing your muscles to stop your wounds from bleeding. Oh well. I'll just recycle it if I roll Resistance again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T09:48:37-07:00","id":123823,"title":"","content":"The beef disarm is actually pretty close to something I have planned for my Nemissary-focused MA style based on allowing others to hurt you in order to deliver a focused offense (though I imagined it more as &quot;locking a blade between your ribs&quot; or something). I was considering making it a standard counter-disarm and a technique rather than a charm, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T21:46:27-07:00","id":124282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms?p=121284#post121284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Investigation:<br /> <br /> <b>Lawman's Sudden Realization</b><br /> If the Solar fails an Investigation roll to identify the culprit of a crime and the criminal begins to plan a second crime in the Solar's general vicinity, the Solar may reroll the Investigation roll in order to gain sudden insight into the culprit's behaviour and stop her before the second crime is committed. In addition, if the Solar uses the Investigation Excellency to enhance the roll, the excellency's cost is reduce by one mote for each of the culprit's crime scenes that the Solar has investigated, successfully or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>To go into greater detail about why I like this Charm so much:<br /> <br /> It introduces a novel way in which Solars can bounce back from failure. Solar Resistance Charms could be seen as doing this (as getting hit is often due to a failure of parrying or dodging), but outside of Solar Resistance and Integrity, I can't remember any Solar Charms that deal with the consequences of failure. Even Solar Resistance and Integrity are about avoiding or rejecting the consequences of failure rather than learning from mistakes or improvising with remaining resources.<br /> <br /> For example, there isn't a Solar Craft Charm which allows the Exalt to take the twisted and ruined product of a failed project and make something useful out of it. There isn't a Melee Charm that allows you to turn a failed parry into a successful defense against the next attack, or perhaps into a counterattack.<br /> <br /> Actually, I'm wondering if you couldn't build an entire Exalted Host around the idea of &quot;come back stronger / learn from mistakes&quot;, and whether or not Solars really should explore this concept space given their power to succeed the first time around.<br /> <br /> But trying to push &quot;succeed the first time around&quot; too far is what led to &quot;solve crimes before they happen / determine guilt before the criminal considers committing the crime&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T06:02:57-07:00","id":124431,"title":"","content":"Craft:<br /> <br /> <b>Instruction of the Celestial Design</b><br /> The Lawgiver writes down the plans and instructions necessary to create a mundane item which she has already crafted once. Anyone who reads and follows the Solar's instructions to craft this item uses the Solar's Attributes, Abilities and Merits rather than their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T09:12:09-07:00","id":125197,"title":"","content":"Survival:<br /> <br /> <b>Mammoth-Stalking Instinct</b><br /> This charm activates when the Solar tracks a mundane animal with higher Strength than her. If the Solar rolls join battle against the animal, she immediately gains momentum equal to the number of threshold successes she rolled on the tracking roll, to a maximum of the difference between the animal's strength and the Solar's strength.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":54,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","user":"Tiresias","date":". 05-04-2014, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T06:59:11-07:00","id":125767,"title":"","content":"Ride: <br /> <br /> <b>Steel-Sundering Charge</b><br /> When the Solar makes a successful close-range Melee, Brawl or Martial Arts attack immediately after moving towards her target, she may add her mount's Strength to the damage roll instead of her own. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T15:59:05-07:00","id":126202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms#post113648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wherein I gaze into the future and write charms for a system I haven't seen yet. This is how I deal with boredom.<br /> <br /> Melee/Brawl:<br /> <br /> <b>Dojo of the Mind</b><br /> The Solar plays out the results of a battle in her mind to create the best opportunity to strike. When activating this Charm, the Solar selects a target. This Charm provides the following effects:<br /> - The Solar's attacks take place only in her mind. Substitute Dexterity for Intelligence and Strength for Wits when rolling attacks and damage.<br /> - The Solar's attacks gains long range.<br /> - The Solar may defend herself and move normally, but may not attack anyone other than her current target.<br /> - The Solar cannot use lethal attacks or Gambits, but can use all her other powers. The Solar's target may defend herself normally.<br /> - The Solar's attacks gain [momentum] as normal. However, they cannot cause effects which require physical contact, such as poison and knockback.<br /> - If the Charm's target attacks the Solar, the Solar immediately gains a clash attack against her.<br /> <br /> Lore:<br /> <br /> <b>Victorious Stratagem Contemplation</b><br /> The Solar studies her opponents in order to understand her weaknesses. The Solar activates this charm when her nemesis rolls battle against someone else. If the Solar witnesses the fight from its beginning to its resolution and takes no other action during that time, she gains (Lore?) momentum the next time she rolls join battle to fight the charm's target.<br /> <br /> Stealth:<br /> <br /> <b>Wing of the Swooping Owl</b><br /> While the Solar is engaged in battle and hidden, he may select one of her opponents as this charm's target. For every round in which the Solar remains hidden from the target, the Solar gains X additional momentum. This charm lasts until the target becomes aware of the Solar.<br /> <br /> Occult:<br /> <br /> <b>Demon-Hunter's Instinct</b><br /> Whenever a spirit uses one of its Charms to harm a mortal within (Essence) miles of the Solar, the Solar may roll Perception + Occult to learn the precise location of both the spirit and its victim.<br /> <br /> Resistance:<br /> <br /> <b>Manna of Flesh and Will</b><br /> Whenever the Solar would gain a point of Willpower, she may instead satiate herself as if she had eaten and slept enough to last a number of days equal to her Essence without requiring further rest or sustenance.<br /> <br /> Medicine:<br /> <br /> <b>Remedy of Exalted Resilience</b><br /> The Solar's supernatural healing skills persist in her absence. When treating a wounded mortal, the Solar may commit a number of motes equal to the lesser of her Intelligence + Medicine or the patient's Stamina + Resistance. So long as the motes remain committed, the patient may apply the benefit of the Resistance Excellency to all attempts to resist poison, disease or death from grievous wounds, adding a number of dice equal to the number of motes committed.<br /> <br /> Ride:<br /> <br /> <b>Steel-Sundering Charge</b><br /> When the Solar makes a successful close-range Melee, Brawl or Martial Arts attack immediately after moving towards her target, she may add her mount's Strength to the damage roll instead of her own.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>&amp; endorsed, I may present some of these to my ST and ask for permission to use them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you think nobody cares if you're alive, try missing a couple of payments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2890-walker-of-ebony-clouds","name":"Walker-of-Ebony-Clouds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T06:24:56-07:00","id":126662,"title":"","content":"Integrity:<br /> <br /> <b>Exemplar of Righteous Will</b><br /> The Solar may activate this charm whenever she successfully resists a social influence using her Resolve and one of her Intimacies. All witnesses who are not directly engaged in the debate automatically gain the Solar's Intimacy as a Minor Intimacy for the rest of the scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T06:57:47-07:00","id":127438,"title":"","content":"Stealth: <br /> <br /> <b>Bound Shadow Steps</b><br /> Whenever the Solar is hidden and following a specific target at close range, she ignores all penalties to her Stealth rolls to remain hidden from her target. She can blend in a crowd and use her environment for cover or to make her presence look completely mundane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T09:09:06-07:00","id":127514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms?p=127438#post127438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stealth:<br /> <br /> <b>Bound Shadow Steps</b><br /> Whenever the Solar is hidden and following a specific target at close range, she ignores all penalties to her Stealth rolls to remain hidden from her target. She can blend in a crowd and use her environment for cover or to make her presence look completely mundane.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This seems a little weak, but we'll need to see what 3e looks like, I guess. It also depends somewhat on how the game contextualizes things -- my experience is that a game has to <i>really </i>drill into your head the importance of using a pile of modifiers all the time before a power that negates non-specific situational penalties becomes useful by itself. As it stands it's always been pretty uncommon for people to apply one-sided penalties to opposed rolls.<br /> <br /> I'm a little wary of blanket penalty negators generally, because they have the tendency to make the game more like a white-room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T06:49:31-07:00","id":128199,"title":"","content":"Craft:<br /> <br /> <b>Inventor's Fleeting Inspiration</b><br /> This charm allows the Solar to work on multiple projects at the same time. The Solar rolls against the project with the highest difficulty and distributes threshold successes across her projects however she wishes. Charms used to enhance the Solar's crafting apply to all projects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T06:26:10-07:00","id":128902,"title":"","content":"Thrown: <br /> <br /> <b>Scattering Starfall</b><br /> The Solar rolls her attack roll against all enemies within close range of her intended target. Enemies who are hit by the attack take Blunt damage, which supersedes the weapon's normal damage tag, and suffer Knockback. If the attack is also used to target a building or other structure, it gains the Piercing tag when dealing damage against it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>